Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] topology: forward changed responses to AL-SAP

The topology-response handler used its boolean result for two unrelated
purposes: whether the IEEE1905 core processed the response and whether the
registered higher-layer entity should receive it.  A response which changed
the core neighbor database returned true after scheduling a Topology
Notification, suppressing AL-SAP data indication.  An unchanged response
returned false and was delivered.  EasyMesh therefore received periodic
client snapshots but not the response carrying a changed wireless backhaul
network membership.

Keep the core database update and standards-defined Topology Notification,
but return false so the normal dispatcher also delivers the original response
to the registered EasyMesh HLE.  The two consumers maintain different state;
successful processing by one must not hide the frame from the other.

The common forwarding routine also selected a topology database using the
remote Ethernet source and then looked up that source/interface MAC as though
it were an AL MAC.  Select the local instance and use the same port lookup as
the response handler so an hwsim interface MAC resolves to its remote Agent;
otherwise even responses deliberately sent to the HLE are silently dropped.

Upstream-Status: Pending
